1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,200
The noble tree house – all natural materials, sturdy construction, aloof from the troubles of the world.
高耸的树屋——全天然材料、坚固的结构、远离尘世的纷扰。

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:19,600
In a more dangerous time in human history, their position above the ground would protect the dweller against environmental difficulties and possible predators.
在人类历史上更危险的时期，它们远离地面，可以保护居住者免受恶劣环境和潜在捕食者的威胁。

3
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:34,100
As modern construction has improved, these arboreal residences have become less of a practical dwelling and more of a children's novelty - a secret den erected in many a back garden.
随着现代建筑技术的进步，这些树木住宅逐渐不再是实用的住所，而更像是孩子们的新奇事物——许多后花园里搭建的秘密巢穴。

4
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:45,040
But now, these fun shelters are appealing to adults too and many are booking themselves in for a few nights among the treetops.
但现在，这些有趣的庇护所也吸引了成年人，许多人会预订在树梢间住上几晚。

5
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:51,410
These tree house hotels can be found from Europe to Australia.
从欧洲到澳大利亚，都能找到这些树屋酒店。

6
00:00:51,410 --> 00:00:55,600
Best of all, they come in a variety of interesting designs!
最棒的是，它们有着各种有趣的设计！

7
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:12,010
From the traditional 'four walls and a roof' habitation, such as at TreeHouse Point, in Washington, North America, to the more artistic Nothofagus Hotel in Chilean Patagonia, whose twelve-sided walls make it look like a beehive.
从传统的“四面墙加屋顶”的住所，比如北美华盛顿的TreeHouse Point，到智利巴塔哥尼亚更具艺术性的Nothofagus酒店，其十二面墙使其看起来像一个蜂巢。

8
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:17,120
If that doesn't appeal, how about a tree pod?
如果这还不够吸引人，那树荚状的树屋呢？

9
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:29,070
The Free Spirit Spheres resort on Vancouver Island in Canada allows guests to stay in one of three yellow spheres, which are suspended from trees.
加拿大温哥华岛的“自由精神球体”度假村允许客人住在三个悬挂在树上的黄色球体中。

10
00:01:29,070 --> 00:01:40,430
The company was founded in 1998 by Tom Chudleigh, who hand built the pods from cedar wood and fibre glass, and then added fixtures and fittings.
该公司由汤姆・查德利（Tom Chudleigh）于1998年创立，他用雪松和玻璃纤维手工建造了这些舱体，然后添加了固定装置和家具。

11
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:45,250
Not only are they as safe as houses, they're popular!
它们不仅像普通房屋一样安全，而且很受欢迎！

12
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:52,110
Visitor numbers have probably doubled in the past five years, Mr Chudleigh tells the BBC.
查德利先生告诉BBC，过去五年里，游客数量可能翻了一番。

13
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:56,300
Digs which are original seem to be a big draw.
独特的住宅似乎很有吸引力。

14
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:01,360
In Sweden, at the Treehotel, numbers have also risen.
在瑞典的树屋酒店（Treehotel），客人数量也在增加。

15
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:07,490
"In 2010, we had four rooms and around 1,500 guests a year.
“2010年，我们有四个房间，每年约1500名客人。

16
00:02:07,490 --> 00:02:11,700
Today we have seven rooms and nearly 5,000 guests,"
如今我们有七个房间，近5000名客人，”肯特・林德瓦尔（Kent Lindvall）解释道。

17
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:18,930
Kent Lindvall explains. Mr Lindvall co-owns the Treehotel with his wife Britta Lindvall.
林德瓦尔先生和妻子布里塔・林德瓦尔（Britta Lindvall）共同经营这家树屋酒店。

18
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:24,940
Each of the domiciles there was designed by an architect, who was asked to make use of the light and surroundings.
那里的每一间住所都由建筑师设计，他被要求充分利用光线和周围环境。

19
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:31,750
Their abodes include a mirrored cube, a bird's nest and a UFO.
他们的居所包括镜面立方体、鸟巢和不明飞行物（UFO）造型的树屋。

20
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:34,790
And how about an office?
那办公室呢？

21
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:46,780
Microsoft, hoping to give its employees thinking space, has commissioned a three-building structure from Pete Nelson, tree house book author and designer and builder of tree houses.
微软希望为员工提供思考空间，委托树屋书籍作者、树屋设计师和建造者皮特・纳尔逊（Pete Nelson）设计了一个由三座建筑组成的树屋办公区。

22
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:53,740
"Studies show people can work better in nature. They are more productive," says Mr Nelson.
“研究表明，人们在自然环境中工作效率更高，”纳尔逊先生说。

23
00:02:53,740 --> 00:03:01,310
If you've no head for heights, then maybe a tree house getaway isn't going to be your home away from home.
如果你恐高，那么树屋度假可能不会成为你的“第二故乡”。

24
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:13,820
But the sense of adventure, the novelty of the setting and the opportunity to return to nature has given an increasing number of tree house-staying adults something to write home about.
但冒险的感觉、环境的新奇感以及回归自然的机会，让越来越多入住树屋的成年人有了值得分享的体验。
